Turns on WinUSB's RAW_IO for librtlsdr's sample stream, on Windows only.
Applied with "git apply" by native/CMakeLists.txt; git apply ignores this header.

Why: on a Windows PC, ADS-B Exchange's MLAT server flagged clock jumps on most of the desktop
feeder's peer pairs (sync table, 7 October 2026), and gave it the maximum bad-sync score, so it
isn't used for positions. The official mlat-client on the same readsb did the same, so the jumps
come from the sample stream, not the MLAT client. The timing precision itself was fine (median
error 0.1 us, as good as a Raspberry Pi feeder at the same site).

The suspected cause: without RAW_IO, WinUSB passes queued reads to the USB stack one at a time, and
in the gap between two reads the RTL2832U's small FIFO can overflow. That loses fewer samples than
readsb's own check notices (it watches for whole 128 KB transfers), but every loss shifts the
sample clock, which is what MLAT measures. RAW_IO keeps all the transfers queued with the host
controller, as Linux's USB stack does. libusb 1.0.30 supports it, but only on request.

The transfers already meet RAW_IO's rules (a multiple of the 512-byte packet size, and no larger
than the pipe's limit, which is checked). readsb's log says whether it took effect.

diff --git a/src/librtlsdr.c b/src/librtlsdr.c
index 82bab6d..1b804de 100644
--- a/src/librtlsdr.c
+++ b/src/librtlsdr.c
@@ -1960,6 +1960,25 @@ int rtlsdr_read_async(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, rtlsdr_read_async_cb_t cb, void *ctx,
 
 	_rtlsdr_alloc_async_buffers(dev);
 
+#ifdef _WIN32
+	/* On Windows, WinUSB hands queued reads to the USB stack one at a time unless RAW_IO is on.
+	 * In the gap between two reads the RTL2832U's small FIFO can overflow: too few samples lost
+	 * for readsb to notice, but each loss is a jump in the sample clock, which MLAT can't use.
+	 * RAW_IO keeps every transfer queued with the host controller, as Linux does. It needs each
+	 * transfer to be a multiple of the packet size (512, checked above) and no larger than the
+	 * pipe's RAW_IO maximum. (ADS-B Exchange Desktop Feeder, native/patches/rtlsdr-winusb-raw-io.patch.) */
+	if (libusb_endpoint_supports_raw_io(dev->devh, 0x81) == 1) {
+		int max = libusb_get_max_raw_io_transfer_size(dev->devh, 0x81);
+		if (max > 0 && dev->xfer_buf_len <= (uint32_t)max && libusb_endpoint_set_raw_io(dev->devh, 0x81, 1) == 0)
+			fprintf(stderr, "WinUSB RAW_IO on for the sample stream (%u-byte transfers, limit %d)\n",
+				dev->xfer_buf_len, max);
+		else
+			fprintf(stderr, "WinUSB RAW_IO not enabled (%u-byte transfers, limit %d)\n", dev->xfer_buf_len, max);
+	} else {
+		fprintf(stderr, "WinUSB RAW_IO not supported for the sample stream\n");
+	}
+#endif
+
 	for(i = 0; i < dev->xfer_buf_num; ++i) {
 		libusb_fill_bulk_transfer(dev->xfer[i],
 					  dev->devh,
